---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProjectPageHeader from '../../components/ProjectPageHeader.astro';
import ProjectSection from '../../components/ProjectSection.astro';
import ProjectList from '../../components/ProjectList.astro';
import ProjectProse from '../../components/ProjectProse.astro';
import TagList from '../../components/TagList.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Base title="Kron / Kacper Noniewicz" description="A Go host that runs sandboxed Lua connectors and automations on a timer or an event.">
  <div class="py-16 pb-20">
    <ProjectPageHeader label="Public / Go / Lua / MIT" title="Kron" intro="One long-lived Kor service that runs Lua connectors and automations. Jobs are plain Lua files in git, triggered by time or by an event, with a sandbox and a run record for every execution." repo="https://github.com/knoniewicz/kron" />

    <div class="max-w-180">
      <ProjectSection title="What it does">
        <ProjectList items={[
          "Two trigger kinds only: time (every, at) and event (on, with prefix wildcards)",
          "Catch-up for daily jobs that were missed while the host was down",
          "A small ctx API: HTTP, JSON, hashing for deterministic ids, Kor calls, Korpus writes and queries, and an optional agent step",
          "Writes an automation.run record for every run, so failures and missed runs are visible",
          "Reloads jobs on SIGHUP; a broken file keeps the old jobs running",
        ]} />
      </ProjectSection>

      <ProjectSection title="How it works">
        <CodeBlock>{`automation "morning-brief" {
  at = "06:00", catchup = true,
  run = function(ctx) ... end,
}`}</CodeBlock>
        <ProjectProse>
          <p>The Lua sandbox has no filesystem, <code class="font-mono text-sm">os</code> or <code class="font-mono text-sm">require</code>. Network goes through <code class="font-mono text-sm">ctx.http_*</code>, environment variables need an allow-list, and every run has a timeout enforced inside the VM and on every call.</p>
        </ProjectProse>
      </ProjectSection>

      <ProjectSection title="Stack">
        <TagList tags={["Go", "Lua", "Kor", "Korpus", "cron"]} />
      </ProjectSection>

      <ProjectSection title="Status">
        <ProjectProse>
          <p>Runs my connectors and automations every day. The engine is open source under MIT; my own jobs live in a separate private repository.</p>
        </ProjectProse>
      </ProjectSection>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
